Dragon Burst (2026-10-27): Burst Limit's declaration-less draws (Renut M2).

The 2D quads (BeginVertices: logos, title, menus) draw with no vertex declaration set: the XDK 6683 Direct3D bound
the vertex shader to one at an earlier draw (0x820B06F8 -> 0x820B05B8 / 0x820B0398), patching its vfetch
instructions in guest memory. The container's own vfetches are unpatched (format 0), so these draws fell to
NoDeclaration and wrote nothing. The draw now reads the inputs from the shader object's patched microcode
(PatchedFetchDeclarationLocked), before the container fallback.

